# SYNTHETIC (Phase 2). Body shape matches GitHub's documented unauthenticated REST rate
# limit exhaustion response; headers modeled on research/site-survey/acl-anthology.md §1/§7
# [LIVE] x-ratelimit-limit: 60 (unauthenticated, per hour) observation on api.github.com
# (the 403-not-429 quirk for GitHub REST rate limiting itself is documented GitHub API
# behaviour, not a live-observed exhaustion -- the survey never actually exhausted the
# budget). HttpClient maps 403 -> no_entitlement by default; the adapter reclassifies ANY
# api.github.com 403 to rate_limited unconditionally (design §6: no read-response-body
# codepath exists since HttpClient doesn't expose headers, so the domain alone decides).
HTTP-STATUS: 403
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
x-ratelimit-limit: 60
x-ratelimit-remaining: 0
x-ratelimit-reset: 1900000000

{"message": "API rate limit exceeded for 203.0.113.5. (But here's the good news: Authenticated requests get a higher rate limit. Check out the documentation for more details.)", "documentation_url": "https://docs.github.com/rest/overview/resources-in-the-rest-api#rate-limiting"}
